-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1116. skip-alone.l4 importing a file, own-eval-b.l4, that has
-- an #EVAL of `taken now` of its own. That #EVAL reads the rule against an empty
-- ledger, and the skip trace here must still read it against its own: one
-- COMMIT, the buy passed over, WITHIN 9, as without the import. (With the clock
-- free it does; with JL4_FIXED_NOW pinned it did not, before the fix.)

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT taken
IMPORT `own-eval-b`

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Bob
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF peek, skip
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    go HAS mode IS A Mode
    buy

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`shop` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY buy PROVIDED NOT `taken now`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS TRUE HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`start` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY go m
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS (IF m EQUALS peek THEN NOT `taken now` ELSE TRUE) HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go skip AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2
